# `web/Dockerfile` runs `npm ci` and then `COPY . .`, so anything here that
# survives into the context is both uploaded and copied *over* what the build
# just installed. `node_modules` alone is 715 MB of the wrong platform's
# binaries; `.next` and `out` are a previous build's output.
#
# The root `.dockerignore` does not cover this: that one applies to a build
# whose context is the repository root, and this image is built from `web/`.
node_modules/
.next/
out/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
playwright-report/
test-results/
.DS_Store
